{"book":"lines-angles","bookTitle":"Lines and angles","concept":3,"title":"Kinds of angles","grades":"Grades 5–6","goal":"I can name kinds of angles by their size.","teach":"An angle measures an amount of turn, in <b>degrees</b> (°). <b>Acute:</b> less than 90°. <b>Right:</b> exactly 90° (marked with a small square). <b>Obtuse:</b> between 90° and 180°. <b>Straight:</b> 180°. <b>Reflex:</b> between 180° and 360°. <b>Revolution:</b> 360°, a full turn.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:148px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 114.0 88.99513267805776\"><g transform=\"translate(-128.0,-53.0)\"><line x1=\"150.0\" y1=\"120.0\" x2=\"220.0\" y2=\"120.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"150.0\" y1=\"120.0\" x2=\"203.6\" y2=\"75.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M172.0,120.0 A22,22 0 0 0 166.9,105.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"192.3\" y=\"109.1\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">acute</text><circle cx=\"150.0\" cy=\"120.0\" r=\"3.2\" fill=\"#444444\"/></g></svg></span><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:148px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 114.0 114.0\"><g transform=\"translate(-128.0,-28.0)\"><line x1=\"150.0\" y1=\"120.0\" x2=\"220.0\" y2=\"120.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"150.0\" y1=\"120.0\" x2=\"150.0\" y2=\"50.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M161.0,120.0 L161.0,109.0 L150.0,109.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"150.0\" cy=\"120.0\" r=\"3.2\" fill=\"#444444\"/></g></svg></span><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:207px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 158.99513267805776 97.62311101832846\"><g transform=\"translate(-83.0,-44.4)\"><line x1=\"150.0\" y1=\"120.0\" x2=\"220.0\" y2=\"120.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"150.0\" y1=\"120.0\" x2=\"105.0\" y2=\"66.4\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M172.0,120.0 A22,22 0 0 0 135.9,103.1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"169.9\" y=\"81.9\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">obtuse</text><circle cx=\"150.0\" cy=\"120.0\" r=\"3.2\" fill=\"#444444\"/></g></svg></span><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:200px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 154.15035054457326 148.35221725867518\"><g transform=\"translate(-87.8,-51.0)\"><line x1=\"150.0\" y1=\"120.0\" x2=\"220.0\" y2=\"120.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"150.0\" y1=\"120.0\" x2=\"109.8\" y2=\"177.3\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M178.0,120.0 A28,28 0 1 0 133.9,142.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"125.5\" y=\"77.5\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">reflex</text><circle cx=\"150.0\" cy=\"120.0\" r=\"3.2\" fill=\"#444444\"/></g></svg></span></div>","ex":{"q":"Name the kind of angle: 95°, 180° and 250°.","steps":["95° is more than 90° but less than 180°: obtuse.","180° is a straight angle.","250° is more than 180° but less than 360°: reflex."]},"watch":"Look at the size, not at how long the arms are drawn. Long arms do not make a bigger angle.","qs":[{"text":"How many right angles make a straight angle?","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Right angles","a":"2","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"90 + 90","steps":"1. Rule: acute is less than 90°; right = 90°; obtuse is between 90° and 180°; straight = 180°; reflex is between 180° and 360°.<br>2. 90° + 90° = 180°, so 2 right angles make a straight angle."},{"text":"What kind of angle is 120°? Circle one.","vis":"","self":1,"parts":[{"label":null}],"hint":"Between 90° and 180°.","steps":"1. Rule: acute is less than 90°; right = 90°; obtuse is between 90° and 180°; straight = 180°; reflex is between 180° and 360°.<br>2. 120° is between 90° and 180°. Answer: C, obtuse."},{"text":"What kind of angle is 270°? Circle one.","vis":"","self":1,"parts":[{"label":null}],"hint":"Between 180° and 360°.","steps":"1. Rule: acute is less than 90°; right = 90°; obtuse is between 90° and 180°; straight = 180°; reflex is between 180° and 360°.<br>2. 270° is between 180° and 360°. Answer: D, reflex."}]}